11. A conjoint reading of Sections 5 and 291 of the Companies Act, 1956 with the definitions in clauses (24), (26), (30), (31), (45) :: 7 ::
M.Cr.C. Nos.10703/2011 & 10832/2011 of Section 2 of that Act would show that the following persons are considered to be the persons who are responsible to the company for the conduct of the business of the company:
(a) the Managing Director(s);
(b) the whole-time Director(s);
(c) the manager;
(d) the secretary;
(e) any person in accordance with whose directions or instructions the Board of Directors of the company is accustomed to act;
(f) any person charged by the Board with the responsibility of complying with that provision (and who has given his consent in that behalf to the Board); and (g) where any company does not have any of the officers specified in clauses (a) to (c),
any Director or Directors who may be specified by the Board in this behalf or where no Director is so specified, all the Directors.
(Emphasis supplied)
12. By reason of the legal fiction introduced by Section 141 of the Act, a person, though, not personally liable for commission of an offence under Section 138 would be vicariously liable therefor.
